"""Read original JDBC/Undo shapes on one owned MySQL instance; preserve unsuccessful driver profiles."""
import argparse
import datetime
import hashlib
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import shutil
import socket
import subprocess
import time
import uuid
from runtime_binding import RuntimeBinding

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
JAVA=ROOT.parent/'seata-java-phase09-oracle'
IMAGE='sha256:a81d043930e51745522bd5c430961cf8286f0a23f0a9a2a6e0108f7ea71b0902'
PASSWORD='seata-mysql-fixture-only'


def sha(path):return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
def read(path):return json.loads(path.read_text('utf-8'))
def need(value,message):
    if not value:raise ValueError(message)


def run(build_dir):
    build_dir=build_dir.resolve();build=read(build_dir/'build.json')
    for row in read(build_dir/'catalog.json')['members']:
        need(sha(build_dir/row['path'])==row['sha256'],'Original build archive differs')
    runtime_build=Path(build['runtime'])
    binding=RuntimeBinding(build_dir,JAVA)
    for row in build['compiled_classes']:
        need(sha(Path(row['path']))==row['sha256'],'Compiled original class differs')
    for row in build['libraries']:
        need(sha(Path(row['path']))==row['sha256'],'Runtime library differs')
    originals=read(build_dir/'source-inputs.json')
    for index,name in enumerate(['rm-datasource','sqlparser/seata-sqlparser-core']):
        original_root=JAVA/name/'target/classes';target=runtime_build/('fallback-'+str(index))
        expected={Path(x['path']).relative_to(original_root):x['sha256'] for x in originals if Path(x['path']).is_relative_to(original_root)}
        need(set(expected)=={p.relative_to(target) for p in target.rglob('*') if p.is_file()},'Fallback file set differs')
        for relative,digest in expected.items():need(sha(target/relative)==digest,'Fallback copied bytes differ')
    stamp=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y%m%d_%H%M%S')+'_'+uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]
    out=ROOT/'docs/phase-2/evidence/undo-java-live'/('run_'+stamp)
    runtime=Path('D:/codex-builds')/('seata_undo_mysql_'+stamp)
    out.mkdir(parents=True);(runtime/'data').mkdir(parents=True);(runtime/'init').mkdir()
    env=os.environ|dict(TEMP='D:/Temp',TMP='D:/Temp',DOCKER_CONFIG='D:/Temp/seata-docker-config',PYTHONUTF8='1',PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE='1')
    for name in ['JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS','JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS','_JAVA_OPTIONS']:env.pop(name,None)
    def put(name,data):
        path=out/name;path.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
        path.write_bytes(data.encode('utf-8') if isinstance(data,str) else data)
    def save(name,value):put(name,json.dumps(value,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
    def command(args,name,check=True,timeout=90):
        value=subprocess.run([str(x) for x in args],cwd=ROOT,env=env,stdout=subprocess.PIPE,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
            creationflags=subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW,timeout=timeout)
        put(name,value.stdout)
        if check:need(value.returncode==0,name+' failed')
        return value
    owner=uuid.uuid4().hex;database='undo_'+owner[:12];name='seata-undo-'+stamp.replace('_','-')
    with socket.socket() as reserved:
        reserved.bind(('127.0.0.1',0));port=reserved.getsockname()[1]
    print('UNDO_JAVA_LIVE '+str(out),flush=True)
    need(json.loads(command(['docker','image','inspect',IMAGE],'image.json').stdout)[0]['Id']==IMAGE,'Cached image differs')
    schema=(Path(__file__).with_name('schema.sql')).read_text('utf-8').replace('__DATABASE__',database)
    original=JAVA/'script/client/at/db/mysql.sql'
    (runtime/'init/00-original-undo.sql').write_bytes(original.read_bytes())
    (runtime/'init/01-oracle.sql').write_text(schema,encoding='utf-8')
    put('original-undo.sql',original.read_bytes());put('fixture.sql',schema)
    paths={Path(__file__),Path(__file__).with_name('runtime_binding.py'),Path(__file__).with_name('schema.sql'),original,ROOT/'docs/phase-2/mysql-undo-format-contract.md'}
    frozen=[]
    for path in sorted(paths):
        snapshot='inputs/'+hashlib.sha256(str(path).encode()).hexdigest()[:24]+'.bin'
        put(snapshot,path.read_bytes());frozen.append(dict(path=str(path),sha256=sha(path),snapshot=snapshot))
    save('source-inputs.json',frozen)
    save('runtime-inputs.json',binding.manifest())
    save('build-binding.json',dict(path=str(build_dir),catalog_sha256=sha(build_dir/'catalog.json'),
        selected_original_sources=len(build['explicit_sources'])-1,compiled_classes=len(build['compiled_classes']),
        runtime_copies_verified=True,fallback_bytes_frozen_not_recompiled=True))
    container=None;profiles=[];cleanup=[]
    env.update(SEATA_MYSQL_PORT=str(port),SEATA_MYSQL_PASSWORD=PASSWORD,SEATA_MYSQL_DATABASE=database)
    try:
        container=command(['docker','create','--pull=never','--name',name,'--label','seata-rust-owner='+owner,
            '--mount','type=bind,source='+(runtime/'data').as_posix()+',target=/var/lib/mysql',
            '--mount','type=bind,source='+(runtime/'init').as_posix()+',target=/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d,readonly',
            '-p','127.0.0.1:'+str(port)+':3306','-e','MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD='+PASSWORD,'-e','MYSQL_DATABASE='+database,
            IMAGE,'--mysql-native-password=ON'],'create.log').stdout.decode().strip()
        save('owned-runtime.json',dict(container=container,owner=owner,image=IMAGE,port=port,database=database,runtime=str(runtime),
            native_password_enabled_for_legacy_oracle_only=True,shared_database=False))
        command(['docker','start',container],'start.log')
        mysql=['docker','exec',container,'mysql','--protocol=TCP','-h127.0.0.1','--default-character-set=utf8mb4','-uroot','-p'+PASSWORD,database,'-N','-e']
        deadline=time.monotonic()+120
        while True:
            value=subprocess.run(mysql+['SELECT COUNT(*) FROM undo_integer_types'],env=env,stdout=subprocess.PIPE,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                creationflags=subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW,timeout=10)
            if value.returncode==0 and value.stdout.rstrip().endswith(b'3'):break
            need(time.monotonic()<deadline,'Owned oracle database not ready');time.sleep(.25)
        command(mysql+["SELECT VERSION(),@@lower_case_table_names; SELECT PLUGIN_NAME,PLUGIN_STATUS FROM information_schema.PLUGINS WHERE PLUGIN_NAME='mysql_native_password';"],'server-before.log')
        command(['D:/Java/jdk-17.0.12/bin/java.exe','-version'],'java-version.log')
        for driver in ['5.1.42','8.0.27']:
            dependency=binding.drivers[driver]
            for profile in ['default','numeric_tinyint']:
                label=driver+'-'+profile;where=runtime/label;where.mkdir()
                binding.verify()
                logging=where/'class-loading.log'
                args=['D:/Java/jdk-17.0.12/bin/java.exe','-Djava.io.tmpdir=D:/Temp','-Duser.home='+str(where),
                    '-Dlogback.configurationFile='+str(runtime_build/'console.xml'),'-Xlog:class+load=info:file='+logging.as_posix(),
                    '-cp',build['classpath']+os.pathsep+str(dependency),
                    'org.apache.seata.rm.datasource.sql.struct.cache.UndoFormatOracle',where,driver,profile]
                value=command(args,label+'/stdout.log',check=False,timeout=60)
                binding.verify()
                for path in where.rglob('*'):
                    if path.is_file():put(label+'/'+path.relative_to(where).as_posix(),path.read_bytes())
                success=value.returncode==0
                loaded=binding.loaded(logging,driver)
                save(label+'/loaded-origin-binding.json',loaded)
                if success:
                    observed=read(where/'observations.json')
                    need(observed['jackson']=='2.18.3' and len(observed['cases'])==6 and observed['driver'].find(driver)>=0,'Wrong original driver/parser profile')
                    log=logging.read_text('utf-8')
                    for typename in ['org.apache.seata.rm.datasource.sql.struct.TableRecords','org.apache.seata.rm.datasource.undo.parser.JacksonUndoLogParser',
                        'org.apache.seata.rm.datasource.sql.struct.cache.MysqlTableMetaCache']:
                        need(any(typename+' source: file:' in line and '/classes/' in line for line in log.splitlines()),'Selected exact original class not loaded from compiled output')
                profiles.append(dict(driver=driver,profile=profile,succeeded=success,exit_code=value.returncode,
                    original_cases=6 if success else 0,driver_sha256=sha(dependency),log=label+'/stdout.log'))
                print('ORIGINAL_JAVA_PROFILE '+label+' '+('passed' if success else 'failed'),flush=True)
        command(mysql+['SELECT COUNT(*) FROM undo_integer_types; SELECT COUNT(*) FROM undo_log;'],'server-after.log')
    finally:
        if container:
            inspect=json.loads(command(['docker','inspect',container],'container-before-cleanup.json').stdout)[0]
            need(inspect['Image']==IMAGE and inspect['Config']['Labels']['seata-rust-owner']==owner,'Refusing cleanup of unowned container')
            command(['docker','logs',container],'container.log',check=False)
            command(['docker','stop','-t','10',container],'stop.log',timeout=30)
            inspect=json.loads(command(['docker','inspect',container],'container-stopped.json').stdout)[0]
            if inspect['State']['Running']:cleanup.append('owned container remains running')
            command(['docker','rm',container],'remove.log')
        save('result.json',dict(profiles=profiles,actual_owned_containers=1,cleanup_errors=cleanup,
            Rust_interop_verified=False,Java_source_case_parity_complete=False,SQL_Undo_atomicity_verified=False,WP05_complete=False))
    need(not cleanup,'Owned container cleanup incomplete')
    binding.verify()
    for row in frozen:need(sha(Path(row['path']))==row['sha256'],'Live source drift')
    members=[dict(path=p.relative_to(out).as_posix(),sha256=sha(p)) for p in sorted(out.rglob('*')) if p.is_file()]
    save('catalog.json',dict(members=members))
    print(json.dumps(dict(run=str(out),catalog_sha256=sha(out/'catalog.json'),profiles_passed=sum(x['succeeded'] for x in profiles))))


if __name__=='__main__':
    parser=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__);parser.add_argument('--build',required=True,type=Path)
    run(parser.parse_args().build)
